('SS1', 'arts', 'Catering Craft', 'Menu planning', 'When planning a meal for a customer with a stated food allergy, what should a caterer do first?', 'Remove the allergen from the menu description only.', 'Assume a small amount is safe for everyone.', 'Check ingredients and prevent cross-contact with the allergen.', 'Use the same unwashed utensils for every dish.', 'C', 'Ingredient checks and preventing cross-contact are essential steps for managing allergy risk.', 'hard', '2', 'true'),
('SS1', 'arts', 'Catering Craft', 'Food storage', 'Which practice is safest for refrigerated leftovers?', 'Leave them uncovered at room temperature overnight.', 'Mix them with raw meat in one container.', 'Store them indefinitely because refrigeration stops all spoilage.', 'Cool and store them promptly in covered, labelled containers.', 'D', 'Prompt cooling and covered, labelled storage help limit contamination and support safe use.', 'medium', '1', 'true')
